  "description": "A vegan version of pasta carbonara that's silky and rich, dotted with meaty bits, plus the characteristic lactic tang of Pecorino Romano, but with no dairy products whatsoever.",
  "notes": "Optional substitutions: cayenne pepper → red chile flakes; white wine vinegar → fresh juice; dry spaghetti → penne\n\nNotes: Use the brine from good-quality fermented sauerkraut—it should be nice and sour. You can also make your own kraut at home and use some of the brine from that. The sauerkraut brine adds the lactic acid that the cheese would normally contribute to the dish, but in a pinch, you could substitute 1/4 cup each of water and dry white wine.",
